# Switch preferred-citation to the Data in Brief article once it is published,
# and add the PLOS ONE article (manuscript PONE-D-26-52711) under references
# when it is accepted and carries a DOI. S.K.M Shadekul Islam's orcid is
# omitted until he supplies it: a CFF validator rejects a doi or orcid field
# that is not one, so these are left out rather than filled with a placeholder.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code or the HACM-10 corpus, please cite the dataset below.
title: "HA-ECN: analysis code for human-model confidence divergence under compound visual ambiguity"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for the HACM-10 corpus. Defines HACM, a signed instance-level
  difference between a model's confidence and elicited human certainty,
  computes it per image across cross-validation folds, and implements the
  three-module system built to reduce the divergence. The corpus itself and
  the trained checkpoints are deposited separately and are linked in by
  assemble.sh.
